      "title": "Troubleshooting Missing Consent Records and Data Residency Mismatches in OAuth Audit Logs",
      "content_summary": "Addresses audit log gaps and incomplete compliance reports caused by missing consent records or data residency flag mismatches within the OAuth Service.",
      "content_body": "When audit logs show missing entries or compliance reports appear incomplete, check for a mismatch in the data residency flags between the OAuth service configuration and the storage layer. This issue is often rooted in data quality problems or unsupported configurations that prevent proper consent record logging. Verify that the current deployment supports the specific residency region defined in the tenant settings. If the configuration is valid, run the standard data repair script to backfill missing consent records. For cases where scripts fail, manual reconciliation of the audit trail against the identity provider's source logs may be required, followed by customer education on correct residency flag setup to prevent recurrence."
